#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:465
msgid "**The title.** `Array.prototype.push()` is a method of every array: you call it as `arr.push(...)`. A title without `prototype`, like `Array.isArray()`, is called on `Array` itself: `Array.isArray(x)`."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:468
msgid "**Syntax.** The ways to call it, one per line. A parameter that appears only in some lines can be left out."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:470
msgid "**Parameters.** What each argument means. \"Optional\" means you may leave it out."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:471
msgid "**Return value.** What the call gives back. For `push`: the new length, not the array - the column \"Returns\" in the table above."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:473
msgid "**Description.** The details. For arrays it says if the method changes the array (\"a mutating method\") or returns a new one - see [Which methods change the array?](#which-methods-change-the-array) below."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:476
msgid "**Examples.** Short code you can paste into the editor and run."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:477
msgid "**Browser compatibility.** Since when the feature works. The table has a column for Node.js too. For a feature newer than ES2020, check that your rule engine supports it."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:505
msgid "The returned values are useful too - an older example with the rainbow:"
msgstr "Върнатите стойности също са полезни - един по-стар пример с дъгата:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:528
msgid "`push` is the method you will write most: it builds a new list, one element at a time. This is how a rule collects the lines of an alert:"
msgstr "`push` е методът, който ще пишете най-често: той строи нов списък, по един елемент. Така правилото събира редовете на един alert:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:543
msgid "**Arrays in memory:** [4. `push` / `pop` / `unshift` / `shift`](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Arrays в паметта:** [4. `push` / `pop` / `unshift` / `shift`](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:546
msgid "`slice` - copy a part"
msgstr "`slice` - копиране на част"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:548
msgid "MDN: [Array.prototype.slice()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/slice)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:550
msgid "`arr.slice(start, end)` returns a **new** array with the elements from `start` up to, **but not including**, `end`. The original array does not change."
msgstr "`arr.slice(start, end)` връща **нов** array с елементите от `start` до `end`, **без да го включва**. Оригиналният array не се променя."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:563
msgid "`end - start` is the number of elements you get. The first three parts of a version:"
msgstr "`end - start` е броят на елементите, които получавате. Първите три части на версия:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:572
msgid "`splice` - remove, insert or replace, in place"
msgstr "`splice` - премахване, вмъкване или замяна, на място"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:574
msgid "MDN: [Array.prototype.splice()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/splice)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:576
msgid "`arr.splice(start, deleteCount, item1, item2, ...)` changes the array **itself**: from index `start` it removes `deleteCount` elements, and puts the new items in their place. It returns the removed elements in a new array."
msgstr "`arr.splice(start, deleteCount, item1, item2, ...)` променя **самия** array: от индекс `start` премахва `deleteCount` елемента и слага новите елементи на тяхно място. Връща премахнатите елементи в нов array."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:594
msgid "Remove **one** element when you know its value - find its index first (section 6):"
msgstr "Премахване на **един** елемент, когато знаете стойността му - първо намерете индекса му (раздел 6):"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:605
msgid "`splice(-1, 1)` when the element is not found"
msgstr "`splice(-1, 1)`, когато елементът не е намерен"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:606
msgid "Without the `if`, `indexOf` gives `-1`, and `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** element - a negative start counts from the end."
msgstr "Без `if`-а `indexOf` дава `-1`, а `splice(-1, 1)` премахва **последния** елемент - отрицателното начало се брои от края."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:610
msgid "`slice` copies, `splice` cuts"
msgstr "`slice` копира, `splice` изрязва"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:611
msgid "The names are almost the same, the effect is not. A way to remember: s**p**lice has an extra letter, and it does extra things - it changes the array."
msgstr "Имената са почти еднакви, ефектът - не. Как да запомните: s**p**lice има една буква повече и прави нещо повече - променя array-я."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:616
msgid "**Array methods:** [1. `slice` and `at`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. `splice`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [7. `splice` in a loop (advanced)](../animations/arrayMethods.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Методи на arrays:** [1. `slice` и `at`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. `splice`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [7. `splice` в loop (advanced)](../animations/arrayMethods.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:621
msgid "Joining arrays: `concat` and spread"
msgstr "Съединяване на arrays: `concat` и spread"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:623
msgid "MDN: [Array.prototype.concat()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/concat), [Spread syntax (...)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Spread_syntax)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:635
msgid "`...arr` (*spread*) \"pours out\" the elements of the array into the new `[ ]`. More about spread in session 6."
msgstr "`...arr` (*spread*) \"изсипва\" елементите на array-я в новите `[ ]`. Повече за spread в занятие 6."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:638
msgid "Which methods change the array?"
msgstr "Кои методи променят array-я?"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:640
msgid "Change the array (*mutating*)"
msgstr "Променят array-я (*mutating*)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:640
msgid "Return a new array or value"
msgstr "Връщат нов array или стойност"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:644
msgid "`reverse`, `sort` (session 7)"
msgstr "`reverse`, `sort` (занятие 7)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:644
msgid "`toReversed`, `toSorted`, `toSpliced` (ES2023)"
msgstr "`toReversed`, `toSorted`, `toSpliced` (ES2023)"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:657
msgid "ES2023+"
msgstr "ES2023+"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:658
msgid "`toReversed()`, `toSorted()`, `toSpliced()` and `with()` are ES2023 - check that your rule engine supports them. `arr.slice().reverse()` gives a reversed copy everywhere."
msgstr "`toReversed()`, `toSorted()`, `toSpliced()` и `with()` са ES2023 - проверете дали rule engine-ът ви ги поддържа. `arr.slice().reverse()` дава обърнато копие навсякъде."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:663
msgid "`delete arr[i]` in old code"
msgstr "`delete arr[i]` в стар код"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:665
msgid "`delete arr[i]` does **not** remove the element - it leaves a hole, and `length` does not change. Use `splice(i, 1)`:"
msgstr "`delete arr[i]` **не** премахва елемента - оставя празно място, а `length` не се променя. Използвайте `splice(i, 1)`:"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:677
msgid "6. Searching: `indexOf`, `includes`, `lastIndexOf`"
msgstr "6. Търсене: `indexOf`, `includes`, `lastIndexOf`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:679
msgid "MDN: [Array.prototype.indexOf()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/indexOf), [Array.prototype.includes()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/includes), [Array.prototype.lastIndexOf()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/lastIndexOf)"
msgstr ""

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:683
msgid "the index of the **first** `x`, or `-1` if there is none"
msgstr "индексът на **първото** `x` или `-1`, ако няма такова"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:684
msgid "the index of the **last** `x`, or `-1`"
msgstr "индексът на **последното** `x` или `-1`"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:685
msgid "`true` or `false` (ES2016)"
msgstr "`true` или `false` (ES2016)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:687
msgid "All three compare with `===`. A second argument tells where to start: `arr.indexOf(x, 3)` searches from index 3."
msgstr "И трите сравняват с `===`. Вторият аргумент казва откъде да започне: `arr.indexOf(x, 3)` търси от индекс 3."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:700
msgid "Allow-lists"
msgstr "Allow-lists"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:702
msgid "In lecture 3 the rule checked the model with `&&`: `if (model !== \"XR-210\" && model !== \"XR-220\") return;`. With five models this line becomes hard to read. An **allow-list** keeps the models in an array:"
msgstr "В лекция 3 правилото проверяваше модела с `&&`: `if (model !== \"XR-210\" && model !== \"XR-220\") return;`. С пет модела този ред става труден за четене. **Allow-list** пази моделите в array:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:717
msgid "Adding a model is now a change in **data**, not in logic. A list of models that must be skipped is a *deny-list* - the same code without the `!`."
msgstr "Добавянето на модел вече е промяна в **данните**, а не в логиката. Списък от модели, които трябва да се пропуснат, е *deny-list* - същият код без `!`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:720
msgid "The same works for any fixed set of values:"
msgstr "Същото работи за всяко фиксирано множество от стойности:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:730
msgid "Old style: `indexOf(...) !== -1`"
msgstr "Стар стил: `indexOf(...) !== -1`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:732
msgid "`includes` arrived in ES2016. Older rules write the same with `indexOf`:"
msgstr "`includes` се появи в ES2016. По-старите правила пишат същото с `indexOf`:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:734
msgid "Older rules"
msgstr "По-стари правила"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:734
msgid "Modern"
msgstr "Модерно"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:739
msgid "**a bug**: misses index 0"
msgstr "**бъг**: пропуска индекс 0"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:748
msgid "`indexOf` and `includes` differ only for `NaN`: `[NaN].indexOf(NaN)` is `-1`, `[NaN].includes(NaN)` is `true`."
msgstr "`indexOf` и `includes` се различават само за `NaN`: `[NaN].indexOf(NaN)` е `-1`, `[NaN].includes(NaN)` е `true`."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:751
msgid "Searching is exact - normalise first"
msgstr "Търсенето е точно - първо нормализирайте"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:761
msgid "`trim()` removes the spaces at both ends, `toUpperCase()` makes capital letters (more in session 8)."
msgstr "`trim()` премахва интервалите в двата края, `toUpperCase()` прави главни букви (повече в занятие 8)."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:764
msgid "`indexOf` on objects"
msgstr "`indexOf` върху обекти"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:765
msgid "`indexOf` and `includes` compare with `===`, so for objects they look for **the same object**, not \"an object with the same keys\": `doc.inventory.enclosures.includes({ id: \"ENC-01\" })` is `false`. To find a record by one of its keys, use a loop (section 10) - or `find` (session 7)."
msgstr "`indexOf` и `includes` сравняват с `===`, затова при обекти търсят **същия обект**, а не \"обект със същите ключове\": `doc.inventory.enclosures.includes({ id: \"ENC-01\" })` е `false`. За да намерите запис по един от ключовете му, използвайте loop (раздел 10) - или `find` (занятие 7)."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:771
msgid "Strings have `indexOf` and `includes` too"
msgstr "И strings имат `indexOf` и `includes`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:772
msgid "`\"4.2.1.7-B00\".includes(\"-\")`, `\"XR-220\".indexOf(\"-\")` (gives 2), `\"4.2.1.7\".at(-1)` and `\"4.2.1.7\".slice(0, 3)` work on strings the same way. More in session 8."
msgstr "`\"4.2.1.7-B00\".includes(\"-\")`, `\"XR-220\".indexOf(\"-\")` (дава 2), `\"4.2.1.7\".at(-1)` и `\"4.2.1.7\".slice(0, 3)` работят върху strings по същия начин. Повече в занятие 8."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:778
msgid "**Array methods:** [3. `indexOf` and `includes`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}; **Algorithms with arrays:** [6. Search with `break` (advanced)](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#6){target=\"_blank\"} - what `indexOf` does inside"
msgstr "**Методи на arrays:** [3. `indexOf` и `includes`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}; **Алгоритми с arrays:** [6. Търсене с `break` (advanced)](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#6){target=\"_blank\"} - какво прави `indexOf` отвътре"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:783
msgid "7. Strings and arrays: `split` and `join`"
msgstr "7. Strings и arrays: `split` и `join`"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:785
msgid "`split` - from a string to an array"
msgstr "`split` - от string към array"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:787
msgid "MDN: [String.prototype.split()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/split)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:789
msgid "`str.split(separator)` cuts the string at every separator and returns an array of the pieces. The separators are dropped. The pieces are always **strings**."
msgstr "`str.split(separator)` разрязва string-а на всеки разделител и връща array от парчетата. Разделителите отпадат. Парчетата винаги са **strings**."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:800
msgid "Three uses you will see in every rule:"
msgstr "Три употреби, които ще видите във всяко правило:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:817
msgid "Versions: from strings to numbers"
msgstr "Версии: от strings към числа"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:819
msgid "`split` gives strings, and strings are compared character by character - `\"10\" < \"9\"` is `true` (lecture 3). Convert every part with `Number` before you compare:"
msgstr "`split` дава strings, а strings се сравняват символ по символ - `\"10\" < \"9\"` е `true` (лекция 3). Преобразувайте всяка част с `Number`, преди да сравнявате:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:835
msgid "This is the first step of `versionBelow` - you write the whole function in session 5. (In session 7 the loop shrinks to `parts.map(Number)`.)"
msgstr "Това е първата стъпка на `versionBelow` - цялата функция ще напишете в занятие 5. (В занятие 7 loop-ът се свива до `parts.map(Number)`.)"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:838
msgid "Packed values: `\"key=value,key=value\"`"
msgstr "Пакетирани стойности: `\"key=value,key=value\"`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:840
msgid "Reports often pack several values into one string. Two splits unpack it: first the list separator, then the key / value separator:"
msgstr "Отчетите често пакетират няколко стойности в един string. Две разделяния ги разпакетират: първо по разделителя на списъка, после по разделителя ключ / стойност:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:859
msgid "A value that contains the separator"
msgstr "Стойност, която съдържа разделителя"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:860
msgid "`\"note=a=b\".split(\"=\")` gives `[ 'note', 'a', 'b' ]` - the value is cut too. Split only at the **first** `=` with `indexOf` and the string `slice`:"
msgstr "`\"note=a=b\".split(\"=\")` дава `[ 'note', 'a', 'b' ]` - стойността също се разрязва. Разделете само на **първото** `=` с `indexOf` и `slice` на string-а:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:870
msgid "(`split` has a second argument, a limit: `\"note=a=b\".split(\"=\", 2)` gives `[ 'note', 'a' ]` - it drops the rest, so it does not help here.)"
msgstr "(`split` има втори аргумент, ограничение: `\"note=a=b\".split(\"=\", 2)` дава `[ 'note', 'a' ]` - останалото отпада, така че тук не помага.)"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:874
msgid "The traps of `split`"
msgstr "Капаните на `split`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:883
msgid "Check the string **before** you split, and clean the pieces:"
msgstr "Проверете string-а **преди** да го разрежете и почистете парчетата:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:899
msgid "`join` - from an array to a string"
msgstr "`join` - от array към string"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:901
msgid "MDN: [Array.prototype.join()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/join)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:903
msgid "`arr.join(separator)` is the opposite of `split`: it glues the elements into one string, with the separator between them. Without an argument the separator is `\",\"`."
msgstr "`arr.join(separator)` е обратното на `split`: слепва елементите в един string, с разделителя между тях. Без аргумент разделителят е `\",\"`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:916
msgid "`join` builds alert texts. Collect the parts with `push`, glue them once at the end:"
msgstr "`join` строи текстовете на alerts. Събирайте частите с `push` и ги слепете веднъж накрая:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:936
msgid "This avoids the classic `text = text + \", \" + item` loop that leaves a stray `\", \"` at the start or the end."
msgstr "Така избягвате класическия loop `text = text + \", \" + item`, който оставя излишно `\", \"` в началото или в края."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:940
msgid "**Array methods:** [4. `split` and `join`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [5. Packed values](../animations/arrayMethods.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Методи на arrays:** [4. `split` и `join`](../animations/arrayMethods.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [5. Пакетирани стойности](../animations/arrayMethods.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:944
msgid "8. Looping over an array"
msgstr "8. Обхождане на array"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:946
msgid "We often need to do the same thing with **every** element. The classic way is a `for` loop over the indexes, from `0` to `length - 1`:"
msgstr "Често трябва да направим едно и също с **всеки** елемент. Класическият начин е `for` loop по индексите, от `0` до `length - 1`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:960
msgid "Write `i < arr.length`, not `i <= arr.length`: the last index is `length - 1`, and `arr[length]` is `undefined`."
msgstr "Пишете `i < arr.length`, а не `i <= arr.length`: последният индекс е `length - 1`, а `arr[length]` е `undefined`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:964
msgid "**Algorithms with arrays:** [1. Traversal with `for`](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Алгоритми с arrays:** [1. Обхождане с `for`](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:967
msgid "In reverse order"
msgstr "В обратен ред"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:969
msgid "Start at the last index, go on while `i >= 0`, step with `i--`:"
msgstr "Започнете от последния индекс, продължете докато `i >= 0`, стъпка `i--`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:982
msgid "The newest entry of a history list is often the last one - walk backwards and `break` at the first match."
msgstr "Най-новият запис в списък с история често е последният - обхождайте назад и спрете с `break` при първото съвпадение."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:986
msgid "**Algorithms with arrays:** [2. Reverse order](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Алгоритми с arrays:** [2. Обратен ред](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:989
msgid "`for...of` - the elements, without the index"
msgstr "`for...of` - елементите, без индекса"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:991
msgid "MDN: [for...of](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/for...of)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:993
msgid "`for...of` (ES2015) gives the elements one by one. Use it when you do not need the index - this is most of the time:"
msgstr "`for...of` (ES2015) дава елементите един по един. Използвайте го, когато не ви трябва индексът - това е в повечето случаи:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1007
msgid "`const` is fine here: every round gets a **new** variable `feature`. (`[i, feature]` is *destructuring* - more in session 6.)"
msgstr "`const` тук е наред: всяко завъртане получава **нова** variable `feature`. (`[i, feature]` е *destructuring* - повече в занятие 6.)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1010
msgid "Use"
msgstr "Използвайте"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1010
msgid "When"
msgstr "Кога"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1012
msgid "you need only the elements - the default"
msgstr "трябват ви само елементите - по подразбиране"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1013
msgid "you need the index, a step other than 1, or two arrays with the same index"
msgstr "трябва ви индексът, стъпка, различна от 1, или два arrays с един и същ индекс"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1014
msgid "backwards, or you remove elements while you loop"
msgstr "назад или когато премахвате елементи по време на обхождането"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1016
msgid "`for...in` is not for arrays"
msgstr "`for...in` не е за arrays"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1017
msgid "`for (const i in arr)` loops over the **keys**: they are strings (`\"0\"`, `\"1\"`, ...), and extra properties (`arr.a` from section 4) come too. Older rules use it on arrays - it works for plain arrays, but `i + 1` gives `\"01\"`, not `1`! Use `for...in` for objects (session 6), `for...of` or `for` for arrays."
msgstr "`for (const i in arr)` обхожда **ключовете**: те са strings (`\"0\"`, `\"1\"`, ...), и идват и допълнителните properties (`arr.a` от раздел 4). По-старите правила го използват върху arrays - работи за обикновени arrays, но `i + 1` дава `\"01\"`, а не `1`! Използвайте `for...in` за обекти (занятие 6), а `for...of` или `for` - за arrays."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1030
msgid "`arr.forEach(function (x) { ... })` - another loop you see in rules - takes a function, so it comes in session 5 and 7."
msgstr "`arr.forEach(function (x) { ... })` - още един loop, който ще видите в правилата - приема функция, затова идва в занятия 5 и 7."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1033
msgid "Example: every element, its square, the sum"
msgstr "Пример: всеки елемент, квадратът му, сумата"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1035
msgid "An old example, with a bug. Run it - which line is wrong?"
msgstr "Стар пример, с бъг. Изпълнете го - кой ред е грешен?"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1058 site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1092 site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1382 site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1464 site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1769
msgid "Answer"
msgstr "Отговор"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1059
msgid "`sum += i` adds the **index**, not the element: 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10. It must be `sum += numbers[i]`. With `for...of` this bug cannot happen: `for (const n of numbers) { sum += n; }`."
msgstr "`sum += i` добавя **индекса**, а не елемента: 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10. Трябва да е `sum += numbers[i]`. С `for...of` този бъг не може да се случи: `for (const n of numbers) { sum += n; }`."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1064
msgid "The accumulator: sum and count"
msgstr "Акумулаторът: сума и брой"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1066
msgid "One variable *collects* the result while the loop runs. Give it the right start value **before** the loop: `0` for a sum or a count, `\"\"` for text, `[]` for a list."
msgstr "Една variable *събира* резултата, докато loop-ът върви. Дайте ѝ правилната начална стойност **преди** loop-а: `0` за сума или брой, `\"\"` за текст, `[]` за списък."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1089
msgid "**Check yourself:** print the sum of all **positive even** numbers in `[-2, 3, 7, 8, -1, 4, 2]`. (Expected: 14.)"
msgstr "**Проверете се:** отпечатайте сумата на всички **положителни четни** числа в `[-2, 3, 7, 8, -1, 4, 2]`. (Очаквано: 14.)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1105
msgid "The same for a range of numbers, without an array (old loop homework): the sum from 1 to 100, and the odd numbers below 100 that divide by 11:"
msgstr "Същото за диапазон от числа, без array (старо домашно за loops): сумата от 1 до 100 и нечетните числа под 100, които се делят на 11:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1125
msgid "**Algorithms with arrays:** [3. Sum of the elements](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Алгоритми с arrays:** [3. Сума на елементите](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1128
msgid "Find elements by a condition"
msgstr "Намиране на елементи по условие"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1130
msgid "The even numbers in an array:"
msgstr "Четните числа в array:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1141
msgid "The negative odd numbers:"
msgstr "Отрицателните нечетни числа:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1153
msgid "The old homework, both tasks at once: the odd numbers, and the odd **positive** numbers:"
msgstr "Старото домашно, двете задачи наведнъж: нечетните числа и нечетните **положителни** числа:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1168
msgid "Collect into new arrays"
msgstr "Събиране в нови arrays"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1170
msgid "Instead of printing, collect the matching elements into a new array with `push`. The task *separateArrayElementsInNewArrays*: the positive even numbers go into one array, the negative odd numbers into another (zero is neither positive nor negative):"
msgstr "Вместо да отпечатвате, съберете съвпадащите елементи в нов array с `push`. Задачата *separateArrayElementsInNewArrays*: положителните четни числа отиват в един array, отрицателните нечетни - в друг (нулата не е нито положителна, нито отрицателна):"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1191
msgid "With the report - the ids of the enclosures that are not on firmware `\"2.14\"`:"
msgstr "С отчета - id-тата на enclosures, които не са на firmware `\"2.14\"`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1205
msgid "**Algorithms with arrays:** [5. Filtering into new arrays](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Алгоритми с arrays:** [5. Филтриране в нови arrays](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1208
msgid "The largest (and the smallest) element"
msgstr "Най-големият (и най-малкият) елемент"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1210
msgid "Take the **first element** as the largest so far, then compare it with every next one:"
msgstr "Вземете **първия елемент** за най-голям засега, после го сравнете с всеки следващ:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1226
msgid "Do not start with 0"
msgstr "Не започвайте от 0"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1227
msgid "`let max = 0;` looks harmless, but with only negative numbers the result is `0` - a value that is not in the array. Start from `arr[0]`. And check first that the array is not empty: `[][0]` is `undefined`."
msgstr "`let max = 0;` изглежда безобидно, но само с отрицателни числа резултатът е `0` - стойност, която я няма в array-я. Започнете от `arr[0]`. И първо проверете, че array-ят не е празен: `[][0]` е `undefined`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1232
msgid "`Math.max(...temps)` gives the same maximum in one line (spread passes the elements as separate arguments; `Math` in session 8) - but not the index."
msgstr "`Math.max(...temps)` дава същия максимум на един ред (spread подава елементите като отделни аргументи; `Math` в занятие 8) - но не и индекса."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1236
msgid "**Algorithms with arrays:** [4. Largest element](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Алгоритми с arrays:** [4. Най-голям елемент](../animations/arrayAlgorithms.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1239
msgid "Search with `break`"
msgstr "Търсене с `break`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1241
msgid "When you need **one** element, stop at the first match:"
msgstr "Когато ви трябва **един** елемент, спрете при първото съвпадение:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1255
msgid "For a plain value this is just `ids.indexOf(\"ENC-03\")`. You write the loop when the condition is more than `===` - for example, \"the first enclosure that is not normal\" (section 10)."
msgstr "За обикновена стойност това е просто `ids.indexOf(\"ENC-03\")`. Loop пишете, когато условието е нещо повече от `===` - например \"първият enclosure, който не е normal\" (раздел 10)."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1259
msgid "Going round in a circle: `%`"
msgstr "Въртене в кръг: `%`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1261
msgid "An old browser example changed a box colour on every click, going round the list of colours. Without the browser, the idea is the index with `% length`:"
msgstr "Стар пример от браузъра сменяше цвета на една кутия при всяко щракване, като обикаляше списъка с цветове. Без браузъра идеята е индексът с `% length`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1273
msgid "The same spreads checks over a list of consoles, one after the other (*round robin*)."
msgstr "Така се разпределят проверки върху списък от конзоли, една след друга (*round robin*)."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1276
msgid "9. Arrays of arrays (two-dimensional)"
msgstr "9. Arrays от arrays (двумерни)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1278
msgid "JavaScript has no real two-dimensional (or multi-dimensional) arrays. But an element can be of any type - also an array - so a table is an **array of arrays**: every element is a row, and every row is an array."
msgstr "В JavaScript няма истински двумерни (или многомерни) arrays. Но елементът може да е от всеки тип - също array - затова таблицата е **array от arrays**: всеки елемент е ред, а всеки ред е array."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1291
msgid "Access: first the row, then the column"
msgstr "Достъп: първо редът, после колоната"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1305
msgid "`matrix[1][1]` is read in two steps: `matrix[1]` gives the row `[\"d\", \"e\", \"f\"]`, and `[1]` of that row gives `\"e\"`."
msgstr "`matrix[1][1]` се чете на две стъпки: `matrix[1]` дава реда `[\"d\", \"e\", \"f\"]`, а `[1]` от този ред дава `\"e\"`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/04-arrays-and-records.md:1309
msgid "**Arrays in memory:** [6. Two-dimensional (advanced)](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}, [7. Shared row (advanced)](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#7){target=\"_blank\"} - why `[row, row]` is a trap"
msgstr "**Arrays в паметта:** [6. Двумерен array (advanced)](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}, [7. Общ ред (advanced)](../animations/arraysInMemory.html#7){target=\"_blank\"} - защо `[row, row]` е капан"

